dcamp.com/search?q=Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/6788067937", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Chestnut+People%2C+Priori+%26+Ludwig+A.F.+V.+2&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 naff"]}, {"t": 6893, "time": "01:54:53", "artist": "Aphex Twin", "title": "Ageispolis", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1668863098", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Aphex+Twin+Ageispolis&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["1992 R&S Records"]}], "counts": {"high": 7, "mid": 5, "low": 5}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:00:00", "end": "00:00:59", "text": "Perspectives they might not encounter in their daily lives. Blurring the lines between mainstream and fringe. Gentlemen, this is Democracy Manifest. Back chat on FBi 94.5. That was Bertie Rinaldi talking to Georgie Gray Spencer and Scott Whitman about the Sydney Fringe Fest and its evolving viewership. but that's all we've got time for today of course a big thank you to our guests dr matthew hill dr will tregonning dr fred betros georgia gray spencer and scott whitmont and a big thanks to our producers james defrayne murphy maya sathi ewan keely and birdie rinaldi this has been back chat we'll be back with the news from your city and beyond next week until then stay tuned for Limsa Kimbo up now"}, {"start": "00:08:30", "end": "00:09:31", "text": "Yes, hello, welcome, show you're dialed to now, it's called Limbs Akimbo, FBi Radio 94.5. My name's Cousin Jackson, gonna take you to midday in a Limbs fashion. That last one, an Australian group that I just found this week, Helen Fransman and Nick Huggins, I guess a duo track was called Sleeping Music this one Jan Jelinek or Jan Jelinek however you want to say it remix hope everyone's doing alright"}, {"start": "00:16:32", "end": "00:16:54", "text": "Underneath us now is Stevia with Wheatfield. It's an alias of Sasuma Yokota. Huge love out to Dale on the line. He's prepping for Father's Day lunch. But says, screw it. I'm pouring a gin and tonic."}, {"start": "00:17:02", "end": "00:17:30", "text": "Coming back after two months to the studios, it feels like I'm in an alternative universe right now. We're in the mirroring studio, I guess while some renovations go down. Some upgrades. First time in maybe five years walking in here and something's different, so maybe the show's a bit different too."}, {"start": "00:17:37", "end": "00:17:56", "text": "It's one of the reasons anyway. If you want to say what's up, 0435123945 is how. At the hubis, maybe in the gonch. Actually, no, in the Sydney side, I guess."}, {"start": "00:21:38", "end": "00:21:54", "text": "There's one amazing one off Balmatt Records. An album called Magic Object. A track's called 22 Halo. A song, 22 Halo."}, {"start": "01:02:44", "end": "01:03:20", "text": "Yeah, this one, Burger Inc. with Elfism. Going out to Ellie. I think she was talking about the Uncle G tune. Feeling swaggy in the old tavern. Back to that person in bed watching the curtains blow. If you want to jump on the text line 0435123945. Just past the hour. It's Limbs Akimbo. Taking you through till noon. You"}, {"start": "01:04:55", "end": "01:05:18", "text": "Our PSA Studio 2 can't handle the sub-bass of Charles AD. Baseline heads, be warned. Hope you guys are feeling it in your cars, on your systems."}, {"start": "01:20:02", "end": "01:20:19", "text": "Sending big, big love out to Joss. Tuning in from the Porno Lounge. Not sure what that is, but I hope you're enjoying. This one, Hard Like a Rock. My last one, Forthcoming Commandee."}, {"start": "01:22:25", "end": "01:22:56", "text": "Yeah, I ended up making another tune with Tiki, Tiki Man, so I'm going to play it for you, but yeah, it's on a new lo-fi fidelity, lo-fidelity, so he sends me demos on WhatsApp audio, so yeah, forgive the, that new beautiful lo-fi compression, hope you dig it regardless, let's try it out."}, {"start": "01:48:58", "end": "01:49:27", "text": "Check, check, one, two. This one underneath us marble. Sending this one out to Angus. The PNR crew, Dem. Out to Harry from Petersham strolling about, too. Out to all those silent listeners. Yeah, if you're just with us and confused. Shows Limbs Akimbo. About ten more minutes left. Hope you're enjoying your day."}, {"start": "01:53:01", "end": "01:53:21", "text": "This one, new one on NAF, it's The Chestnut People. I think it's number five. One, maybe two more if we're lucky. Hope you've enjoyed the show. Until next time, it's Limbs Akimbo, FBi."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:07:00"}, "track": {"title": "Unstet-Schleifen (Jan Jelinek Remix)", "artists": [{"name": "Kammerflimmer Kollektief"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "f